# Repository (Spring Data JPA)

Repositories are **interfaces** that extend Spring Data JPA's `JpaRepository`. Spring auto-generates the implementation at runtime.

## Structure

```java
// src/main/java/com/duoc/LearningPlatform/repository/OrderRepository.java

import org.springframework.data.jpa.repository.JpaRepository;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Repository;

@Repository
public interface OrderRepository extends JpaRepository<Order, Long> {

    List<Order> findByStatus(OrderStatus status);

    Optional<Order> findByCustomerNameAndStatus(String customerName, OrderStatus status);
}
```

## Spring Data Method Naming

Spring generates queries from method names. Use this convention:

| Keyword | Example | Generated SQL |
|---------|---------|---------------|
| findBy | `findByName(String name)` | `WHERE name = ?` |
| findAllBy | `findAllByStatus(Status s)` | `WHERE status = ?` |
| countBy | `countByStatus(Status s)` | `SELECT COUNT(*) WHERE status = ?` |
| existsBy | `existsByEmail(String email)` | `SELECT EXISTS WHERE email = ?` |
| deleteBy | `deleteByStatus(Status s)` | `DELETE WHERE status = ?` |

### Combining conditions

```java
List<Order> findByStatusAndCustomerName(OrderStatus status, String name);
List<Product> findByPriceGreaterThan(double price);
List<Student> findByNameContainingIgnoreCase(String name);
List<Order> findByStatusOrderByCreatedAtDesc(OrderStatus status);
```

## Custom Queries

For complex queries that method naming can't express:

```java
@Repository
public interface ProductRepository extends JpaRepository<Product, Long> {

    @Query("SELECT p FROM Product p WHERE p.price BETWEEN :min AND :max")
    List<Product> findByPriceRange(@Param("min") double min, @Param("max") double max);
}
```

## Built-in Methods from JpaRepository

No need to declare these — they come for free:

| Method | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| `save(entity)` | Insert or update |
| `findById(id)` | Find by primary key (returns `Optional`) |
| `findAll()` | Get all entities |
| `deleteById(id)` | Delete by primary key |
| `count()` | Count total records |
| `existsById(id)` | Check existence |

## Non-Negotiable Rules

### ❌ I will NEVER:
1. Put business logic in repositories
2. Write raw SQL when Spring Data method naming suffices
3. Create repository implementations manually (Spring generates them)
4. Return DTOs directly from repositories (return entities)

### ✅ I will ALWAYS:
1. Extend `JpaRepository<Entity, IdType>`
2. Use Spring Data method naming conventions for simple queries
3. Use `@Query` only for complex queries that method naming can't handle
4. Annotate with `@Repository`
5. Use `Optional` return types for single-entity lookups
